  "caption": "Quinn's knees sound like a drum kit on every squat, and the knuckles do the encore. Then someone said cracking causes arthritis. Cue a week of quiet worry.\n\nGood news: most joint noises are harmless. Gas bubbles, tendons flicking over bone and normal friction can all make sounds, and painless noise doesn't predict damage. Knuckle cracking included.\n\nWhat often helps: keep training if clicky knees are pain-free, build strength around noisy joints, tweak the load if a tendon keeps snapping, and go easy on forceful neck self-cracking. No need to chase silence.\n\nNoise that comes with pain, swelling, locking or giving way, or a loud pop during an injury, is worth getting checked.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
